    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39570" root="ند" body-key="n">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَادٌّ</span></b> , act. part. n. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَدَّ</span>, A camel <i>taking fright,</i>
or <i>shying, and running away, at random; &amp;c.:</i>
pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نِدَادٌ</span>: (Msb, TA:) and quasi pl. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَدَدٌ</span>;
(L;) signifying camels <i>in a state of dispersion.</i>
(L, K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَيْسَ لَهُ نَادٌّ</span> <i>He has not any means of
subsistence:</i> (K:) app. meaning live stock; from
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَدَّ</span>, said of a camel. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَاذٌّ</span>,
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اَشَذَّهُ</span>.]

